stent with a Safe Democratic rating.", "watch": "A major late scandal or an unusually favorable Republican national environment could narrow the margin, though the race's outcome is unlikely to change.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Wes Moore (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Wes Moore seeks a second term against 2022 rematch opponent Dan Cox, a far-right Republican who lost decisively four years ago. Maryland's D+15 partisan lean and Moore's incumbency give him a strong structural edge, and every major race rater places the contest in the Solid or Safe Democratic column.\n\nThe most recent live-caller poll, from UMBC in late September, shows Moore ahead 51-24, a 27-point margin. Moore has raised over $15 million and holds $6.5 million on hand, while Cox has raised under $250,000. Prediction markets price Moore's chances near 98%. Cox has tried to focus the race on taxes, energy costs, and affordability in their October debates, but there is little evidence he has moved the numbers. Moore remains a heavy favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 19.52}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9967, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9939, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9959, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9942, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9961, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9947, "margin": 20.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margin": 23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.994, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9986, "margin": 23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9974, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "